    "title": "Laminators sold on Amazon recalled for fire risk - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zach Kaplan ,\n31 minutes ago\n( NewsNation ) — A Minnesota company is voluntarily recalling more than 50,000 Scotch-branded laminators following reports of them catching fire, federal regulators announced Thursday.\nThe recalled thermal laminators were sold online on Amazon from June 2024 through September 2026 for between $44 and $56, according to the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission .\nAmazon recalled 113K bottles of acetaminophen tablets over discoloration The CPSC announced the recall after 3M Company \"received 63 reports of the laminators smoking, melting and overheating, including five reports of the laminators catching fire and one report of minor property damage.\"\nConsumers should stop using the recalled product, unplug it and head to this website for a refund. While the laminators can overheat and pose a fire hazard, there have been no reported injuries so far.\nFor questions, consumers can contact the company at 800-772-4337 during standard business hours.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "( NewsNation ) — A Minnesota company is voluntarily recalling more than 50,000 Scotch-branded laminators following reports of them catching fire, federal regulators announced Thursday. The recalled thermal laminators were sold online on Amazon from June 2024 through September 2026 for between $44 and $56, according to the U.S. Consumer Product Safety Commission . Consumers should stop using the recalled product, unplug it and head to this website for a refund. While the laminators can overheat and pose a fire hazard, there have been no reported injuries so far.",
